<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 72,753 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 72,753 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 72,753 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 89,355 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 6,959	   14,945</p>
<p>    Import cargo			65,794	   74,410</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, eight ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours four ships were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Crystal River    23/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Konpolis	   22/10</p>
<p>Sugar		     1,400	 Gemstar-1	  26/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage  22/10</p>
<p>Soya bean oil	  11,500	 Red Azalea	 21/10</p>
<p>Sulphur		   5,000	 Calimenesti	  due</p>
<p>Gas oil		  28,000	 Fair Seas	  18/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
